@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam object {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #4338CA
  FontColor #111827
}

title Modal μ-calculus syntax: the νX binder and its positive bound variable

' ── The abstract syntax tree of  ag φ = νX.(φ ∧ [-]X) ───────────────────────
' Root is the fixpoint binder; the body is a conjunction of a state
' proposition φ and a box modality whose operand is the bound variable X.
object "νX  (fixpoint binder)" as Binder #FEF3C7
object "∧  (conjunction)" as And
object "φ  (state proposition)" as Phi
object "[-]  (box modality)" as Box
object "X  (bound fixpoint variable)" as XVar #DCFCE7

' parse-tree edges (parent --> child)
Binder --> And
And --> Phi
And --> Box
Box --> XVar

' ── The binding back-edge: the leaf X refers to the enclosing νX binder ──────
XVar ..> Binder : bound; positive occurrence (even ¬-depth) ⟹ Φ monotone (Lemma 3.3)

note right of And #E0E7FF
  a fixpoint variable ranges over state-sets (2^S),
  a separate namespace from relational variables.
end note

legend right
|= Color |= Role |
|<#FEF3C7> | the νX greatest-fixpoint binder (least/greatest fixpoint head) |
|<#DCFCE7> | the bound fixpoint variable leaf X (recurs into the binder) |
|<#E0E7FF> | annotation / scoping law |
endlegend
@enduml
